"MCP_PROMPT" = "You can control an iPhone through the iOS MCP service. See the tool list for capabilities and parameters; the following notes cover common pitfalls and conventions.\n\nMCP URL: %@\n\nUsage notes:\n1. Start with describe_screen: it returns the foreground app, tappable elements, and exact coordinates together, making it the token-efficient default for checking the current screen. Screenshot and OCR are excluded by default; enable include_screenshot / include_ocr explicitly when needed.\n2. Use lower-level screen tools when you need more control: get_ui_elements (visible_only / limit / debug) for off-screen/non-tappable nodes, result limits, or AX debugging; ocr_screen (region / fast / languages) for content AX cannot see (games, Flutter/RN/Unity, Canvas, text in images), a specific region, faster scans, or language selection.\n3. screenshot uses the most tokens. Use it when AX and OCR are insufficient or you actually need the image, not after every action. Parse image content: base64 is in result.content[0].data and mimeType is image/jpeg. Do not read result.content[0].text.\n4. All these screen-reading tools use screen points. Pass OCR/AX coordinates directly to tap_screen / long_press without conversion.\n5. If get_screen_info shows locked=true/screen_on=false, or the screenshot looks like the Lock Screen, stop normal app automation. Call wake_and_home, then verify with get_screen_info/describe_screen (or screenshot if needed). Do not substitute a single press_home: on a locked device it usually only wakes the screen or opens the unlock prompt.\n6. The server enforces a lock guard. When locked or the screen is off, interactive/write tools such as taps, swipes, text input, app launch, and Shell are blocked; only observation, screenshots, and recovery tools such as wake_and_home are allowed.\n7. Prefer tap_element by text/label or use UI node coordinates. Read the UI again after a page change, or use wait_for_element before proceeding.\n8. Try input_text first. If it fails, times out, or returns isError, immediately retry the same text with type_text instead of repeating input_text.\n9. read_file has a size limit. Use GET /download_file for complete large or binary files.\n10. Installing IPA/DEB: upload computer-local files with POST /upload_file first, then pass the returned device path to install_app (IPAs can be unsigned). To uninstall, use bundle_id for apps and package_id for DEBs.\n11. install_app only installs local .deb files and does not download dependencies. Upload and install any third-party dependencies first.\n12. Successful DEB installation/removal restarts SpringBoard. Wait a few seconds, then make one bounded /health check, for example: curl -sS --connect-timeout 3 --max-time 5 %@. If polling is needed, use while/seq, not brace expansion such as for i in {1..30}.";
